# hdr_sweep_budget_2026-08-05 — provenance

host: WSL2 dev box, AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (28 threads visible, ~59 GiB), NO -C target-cpu=native (runtime SIMD dispatch)
date: 2026-08-05 (UTC 2026-08-06 01:30-04:30)
sources: /mnt/v/output/imazen-26-hdr-grid-2026-06-14 (16-bit PQ PNG, cICP {1,16,0,1}; the PLAN_HDR 76-source rendition grid)
  - 1069_general_illuminated-castle-night (portrait; night, extreme dynamic range)
  - 1233_interiors_cathedral-ceiling-interior (landscape; interior, blown windows)
  - 1493_nature_sunset-over-sea (landscape; smooth sky gradient + sun)
size ladder (64-aligned, native pyramid levels + one real-pixel 64x64 center crop of the 0.2 MP level):
  64x64 (4,096 px) | 192x256 (49,152) | 384x512 (196,608) | 768x1024 (786,432) | 1536x2048 (3,145,728) | 2304x3072 (7,077,888)
quality grids (21 points each):
  zenav1-svt  CQP qp 1,4,7,...,60,63 (qp0=lossless is refused by the port)
  zenjxl / zenavif / uhdr  generic quality 0,5,10,...,100
preset/effort axis (extended 2026-08-05 to the FASTEST tier per user directive):
  zenav1-svt presets 6 (quality), 10, 13 (fastest; SpeedConfig max) + a 2-size x 5-qp HdrFork spot check
  zenjxl effort 7 (crate default) + effort 1 (fastest)
  zenavif rav1e speed 4 (adapter default) + speed 10 (fastest)
  uhdr base-JPEG quality is the swept knob; gainmap q85 / scale 4 fixed (crate defaults)
coverage: 18 (source,size) cells per fit for all 7 primary arms; zenrav1e-sdefault 16-18
  (truncated: sources 1+2 complete, source 3 small tiers only — superseded mid-run by the
  speed-10 arm when the preset axis was extended); svt-p6-fork 2 (spot check). Per-row n_points
  is carried in the committed TSV.
reps: 64x64 ->5, <=0.79MP ->3, >=3.1MP ->2; median per cell; untimed warmup per (bin,size) at median q
threading: RAYON_NUM_THREADS=1; cpu_ms/wall ratio recorded per cell (all arms ~=1.0 => single-threaded)
harness: ~/tmp scratch workspace `hdrbench` (4 bins calling the real encoder APIs in-process; the
  jxl/avif bins mirror zenmetrics-cli sweep/hdr.rs encode_jxl_hdr/encode_avif_hdr verbatim; the svt bin
  feeds try_encode_frame_420_hbd with BT.2020nc limited-range 10-bit 4:2:0 converted from the PQ code values)
metric timing: zenmetrics score-pairs --hdr --gpu-runtime cuda on (ref,ref) same-dims pairs,
  1-row vs 9-row invocations; marginal = (wall9-wall1)/8; GPU = RTX 5070

